[33.72343, "o", "\u001b[0m← \u001b[0mWrite jq_args.yaml\r\nCreated file successfully: jq_args.yaml\r\n"]
[35.597106, "o", "> build · deepseek-v4.1-flash\r\n"]
[37.218796, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mcd /app && jq $(yq -r '.args[]' /app/jq_args.yaml) \"$(yq -r '.filter' /app/jq_args.yaml)\" /app/users.json > /tmp/verify.json && diff /tmp/verify.json /app/active_users_report.json && echo MATCH; jq -r '[.[] | .status] | unique | join(\",\")' /app/users.json; jq '[.[] | select((.last_login|length) != 10 or (.user_id|type) != \"number\")] | length' /app/active_users_report.json; jq -r '.[].username' /app/active_users_report.json | sort -c && echo SORTED_OK\r\nMATCH\r\nactive,inactive,pending\r\n0\r\nSORTED_OK\r\n"]
[39.032461, "o", "> build · deepseek-v4.1-flash\r\n"]
[41.554323, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mcd /app && jq 'map(select(.status==\"active\") | {user_id:.id,username:.username,email:.email,last_login:(.last_login[0:10]),role_count:(.roles|length),primary_role:(.roles[0] // null)}) | sort_by(.username)' users.json > /tmp/expected.json && diff /tmp/expected.json active_users_report.json && echo EQUIVALENT_OK; jq '[.[]|select(.status==\"active\")]|length' users.json; jq -r 'to_entries[0].value' jq_args.yaml 2>/dev/null | head -1\r\nEQUIVALENT_OK\r\n346\r\n"]
[43.276743, "o", "> build · deepseek-v4.1-flash\r\n"]
[43.523317, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mcd /app && cat cmd.sh && cat jq_args.yaml && ls -l cmd.sh jq_args.yaml active_users_report.json\r\njq --indent 2 'map(select(.status == \"active\") | {user_id: .id, username: .username, email: .email, last_login: (.last_login | split(\"T\")[0]), role_count: (.roles | length), primary_role: (if (.roles | length) > 0 then .roles[0] else null end)}) | sort_by(.username)' /app/users.json > /app/active_users_report.json\r\nfilter: \"map(select(.status == \\\"active\\\") | {user_id: .id, username: .username, email: .email, last_login: (.last_login | split(\\\"T\\\")[0]), role_count: (.roles | length), primary_role: (if (.roles | length) > 0 then .roles[0] else null end)}) | sort_by(.username)\"\r\nargs:\r\n  - \"--indent 2\"\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 61820 Nov  1 00:49 active_users_report.json\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root   316 Nov  1 00:49 cmd.sh\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root   289 Nov  1 00:49 jq_args.yaml\r\n"]
[45.650097, "o", "> build · deepseek-v4.1-flash\r\n"]
[47.878875, "o", "All three files are created and verified.\r\n\r\n**What was done**\r\n\r\n- **`/app/active_users_report.json`** — 346 active users, each with:\r\n  - `user_id` from `id`, `username`, `email`\r\n  - `last_login` truncated to `YYYY-MM-DD`\r\n  - `role_count` = length of `roles`\r\n  - `primary_role` = first role, or JSON `null` when `roles` is empty\r\n  - Sorted ascending by `username`, formatted with 2-space indentation (`--indent 2`)\r\n\r\n- **`/app/cmd.sh`** — the exact command executed:\r\n  ```sh\r\n  jq --indent 2 'map(select(.status == \"active\") | {...}) | sort_by(.username)' /app/users.json > /app/active_users_report.json\r\n  ```\r\n\r\n- **`/app/jq_args.yaml`** — `filter` holds the full jq expression and `args` contains `\"--indent 2\"` only (no command, filter, or file paths).\r\n\r\n**Verification performed**\r\n\r\n- Rebuilt the command exactly as specified (`jq $(yq -r '.args[]' …) \"$(yq -r '.filter' …)\" /app/users.json > …`) and confirmed the output is byte-identical to the report.\r\n- Cross-checked with an independently wri"]
[47.878947, "o", "tten jq filter using `.[0:10]` and `// null` — identical output.\r\n- Confirmed usernames are strictly sorted, and that the active-user count matches the source (346).\r\n"]
